To speed up the JSON parser, you can implement caching for previously parsed values. This would reduce the need to repeatedly construct lists and dictionaries, which is a common bottleneck in JSON parsing. You can use a dictionary to store the results of these recursive calls, so that if a value has already been parsed, it can be returned directly instead of being re-parsed.

